<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyle, Ayrshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyle is a historic district of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayrshire">Ayrshire</a> in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, lying between the rivers Irvine and Doon. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was part of the Brittonic north; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eadberht-of-northumbria">Eadberht of Northumbria</a> annexed it in 750, extending Northumbrian rule westward. In later centuries it was divided into King's Kyle and Kyle Stewart and remained a district of Ayrshire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyle-ayrshire.jpg" alt="Kyle, Ayrshire" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benson85 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kyle_(district).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
